    "summary": "New src/daemon/steps/host.ts: STEP_TOOL_NAMES (the seven tools), stepToolTable (insrc_analyze -> runAnalyzeOneShot, insrc_analyze_step, insrc_workflow_step, insrc_build_step, insrc_triage -> their handlers; insrc_review_step -> handleReviewStep(args, { signal }); insrc_code_review_step -> handleCodeReviewStep(args, { ...withStepClient(DEFAULT_DEPS), signal }), which also closes the t6 gate's note that withStepClient had no production caller) and createStepCallHandler. The handler checks the tool against the table (own keys only, so '__proto__'/'toString' are unknown) and answers 'step-unknown-tool'; checks the context (cwd required, envRepo string, client claude|codex) and answers 'step-failed' when malformed; runs the tool inside runInStepContext(context) with the stream's signal; sends one 'done' frame whose data is the handler's envelope object itself, or 'step-failed' with the thrown message. src/daemon/index.ts registers 'step.call' in its stream map (dynamic import, handler built once). The four moved state stores (analyze, workflow, review incl. its update path, code-review) now say the insrc daemon was restarted and the run must be started again with phase='start'. Tests: the equivalence test runs all seven real handlers on a temporary graph and vector store, once directly and once through step.call, and compares the envelopes with only the fresh state token normalised; the cancellation test serves step.call through the real IpcServer connection handling on a temporary socket and destroys the client socket during a design-review wait and a code-review wait, and the inner review handlers see their signals abort. Falsifying mutations (no context, either signal dropped, envelope altered, a miss message reverted) each fail a test. Full sweep in docs/epics/complete-consistent-richer-code-index-one-E20261011c2ba6fa6/S011/sweeps.md: nothing newly failing from this task (two git-maintenance.lock flakes outside the task, 3 of 3 alone).",
